# E404 Kernel for Xiaomi Pad 6 (pipa) — HyperOS 4.0

Stable HyperOS 4.0 port branch for the Xiaomi Pad 6 (`pipa`).

This repository is based on the E404 `staging-bpf` kernel tree and carries the
Android 16/17 backports, HyperOS input changes, and 4.19 compatibility work
needed by this port.

```text
Stable branch: HyperOS4.0-404-stable
Base tree:     kvsnr113/xiaomi_sm8250_kernel_e404
Base branch:   staging-bpf
Device:        Xiaomi Pad 6 (pipa)
Reference ROM: HyperOS 4.0.8.0
Kernel source: Linux 4.19.404R
SukiSU Ultra:  v4.3.0
SUSFS:         v1.5.9
```

The user-visible UTS release is intentionally spoofed for Android 16/17
compatibility. The actual source base and build configuration are 4.19.

## Included changes

This branch includes the HyperOS 4 port bring-up and the following compatibility
and reliability work:

- Android 16/17 BPF instruction support, vendor hooks, and related tree-wide
  backports.
- HyperOS touch, pen connection strategy, refresh-rate switching, touch reset
  recovery, and Xiaomi Pad 6 touchpad scale fixes.
- Millet cgroup and binder support.
- Built-in SukiSU Ultra v4.3.0 with SUSFS v1.5.9.
- 4.19 SukiSU hooks for manager fd installation, seccomp handling, allowlist
  loading, `init.rc` injection, and the preinit runner.
- 4.19 SUSFS compatibility helpers and SELinux status hiding.
- 4.19 `mount_hide` support. The three proc mount show helpers are linked
  directly instead of relying on runtime kallsyms lookup.
- PowerHAL compatibility sysctls:
  - `sched_min_task_util_for_boost`, default `51`
  - `sched_min_task_util_for_colocation`, default `35`

`CONFIG_KSU_FEATURE_ADBROOT` and KPM are intentionally disabled. Some newer
SUSFS features are not available in the pinned v1.5.9 implementation.

## Configuration

The complete, validated configuration is stored in:

```text
arch/arm64/configs/vendor/pipa_hos4_defconfig
```

Important options:

```text
CONFIG_KSU=y
# CONFIG_KSU_FEATURE_ADBROOT is not set
# CONFIG_KPM is not set

CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS=y
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_PATH=y
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_MOUNT=y
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_KSTAT=y
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SPOOF_UNAME=y
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_ENABLE_LOG=y
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_HIDE_KSU_SUSFS_SYMBOLS=y
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SPOOF_CMDLINE_OR_BOOTCONFIG=y
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_OPEN_REDIRECT=y
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_MAP=y

CONFIG_SECCOMP=y
CONFIG_SECCOMP_FILTER=y
CONFIG_LTO_CLANG_THIN=y
CONFIG_SCHED_TUNE_DUMMY=y
# CONFIG_KALLSYMS is not set
```

## Build environment

The validated build used:

```text
Ubuntu 26.04 LTS
Ubuntu clang version 20.1.8
Ubuntu LLD 20.1.8
GNU aarch64 cross binutils
LLVM=1
LLVM_IAS=1
```

Install the usual kernel build dependencies and a matching Clang/LLD toolchain.
The build also needs Python 3, bc, bison, flex, cpio, gzip, lz4, zstd, libssl,
libelf, rsync, git, and `aarch64-linux-gnu-*` binutils.

## Build

Use a clean output directory. For this branch, export the kernel UAPI headers in
the layout expected by the integrated SukiSU build:

```sh
export PATH="/usr/lib/llvm-20/bin:$PATH"

make O=out ARCH=arm64 vendor/pipa_hos4_defconfig

make O=out ARCH=arm64 \
  headers_install \
  INSTALL_HDR_PATH="$PWD/out/usr/out/usr"

mv out/usr/out/usr/include out/usr/include
mv out/usr/out/usr/techpack out/usr/techpack

make O=out ARCH=arm64 \
  CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- \
  LLVM=1 LLVM_IAS=1 \
  KSU_GITHUB_VER=4.3.0 \
  -j"$(nproc)" Image
```

Output:

```text
out/arch/arm64/boot/Image
```

This is a raw ARM64 kernel `Image`, not an Android `boot.img`.

## Packaging and installation

Use an AnyKernel3 installer for recovery installation. The validated package
uses the known-good `vendor_boot.img` and `dtbo.img` together with the new kernel
Image. Do not write the raw `Image` directly to `boot`.

Validated reference build from 2026-11-02:

```text
kernel SHA256:
D716EDC785200D1F005BDF8E421095C1322BB76FF8AA16F46D506243E47AB1C8

AnyKernel ZIP SHA256:
AD5B6FD5BF102F291728F9AFA2CC694E9A7B4AD98745BC4A3625D0500FE5A20A
```

## ROM-side note

The tested ROM uses a cleaned ODM image without the MSLG/PC Linux desktop
support. On this 4.19 tree, file-backed loop devices returned `EIO` when backed
by F2FS/EROFS, which caused `mslgrootfs` to restart repeatedly. The working
fallback required staging the 475 MB image in tmpfs, increasing boot time and
memory use. Removing MSLG from ODM was the safer choice for this ROM.

This cleanup is separate from the kernel repository and is not applied by
flashing the AnyKernel ZIP.

